    "module": {
      "purpose": "Provides a cached async lookup mapping normalized React error messages to GitHub issue search results using React's experimental cache and suspense-like thenables.",
      "summary": "This module implements a small caching layer for React DevTools ErrorBoundary. It normalizes error messages by stripping numeric Fiber IDs, then uses React's unstable_getCacheForType to store a per-error thenable. The thenable supports both React.use (Suspense) and manual status inspection. A GitHub API call is made on cache miss, with callbacks to fulfill or reject the thenable, plus a setTimeout fallback that rejects after 3000ms. The module exports a single finder function and keeps internal helpers for cache map creation and record reading.",
      "businessContext": "Powers React DevTools error suggestions by linking runtime errors to GitHub issues. Failure means users get no contextual issue links.",
